asr-000140
00:59:07.060 --> 00:59:10.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We are living at a time when the peso is at its slowest,

asr-000141
00:59:10.600 --> 00:59:12.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: while inflation rates are on the rise.

asr-000142
00:59:13.620 --> 00:59:17.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Our economy grew by only 4.4% in 2025,

asr-000143
00:59:17.680 --> 00:59:20.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and growth has remained weak this year.

asr-000144
00:59:20.260 --> 00:59:21.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Inflation remains elevated,

asr-000145
00:59:22.460 --> 00:59:24.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: reaching 6.1% in August,

asr-000146
00:59:25.240 --> 00:59:27.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and while the poverty rate has declined,

asr-000147
00:59:27.400 --> 00:59:28.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: more than 11 million

asr-000148
00:59:28.640 --> 00:59:31.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Filipinos are still living below the poverty line.

asr-000149
00:59:32.860 --> 00:59:37.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: These numbers should remind us that economic growth cannot be measured by statistics alone.

asr-000150
00:59:37.980 --> 00:59:42.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ang tunay na sukatan ay kung gumaan ba ang buhay ng ating makababayan.

asr-000151
00:59:43.220 --> 00:59:46.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: This is where DEP-DEB plays an important role.

asr-000152
00:59:47.340 --> 00:59:49.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: You help determine where our country is going,

asr-000153
00:59:49.860 --> 00:59:51.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: which investments we should prioritize,

asr-000154
00:59:52.040 --> 00:59:57.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and which programs and infrastructure projects will produce the greatest and most lasting benefit

asr-000155
00:59:57.380 --> 00:59:58.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: for our people.

asr-000159
00:59:59.300 --> 01:00:12.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: DepDEP will also be the primary government agency to oversee and ensure the fulfillment of the promises of the Master Plan for Infrastructure and National Development, or the MIND Act, once it becomes a law.

asr-000160
01:00:13.620 --> 01:00:20.600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I'm very hopeful that whatever budget given to DepDEP will aid them in preparing for the implementation of the MIND Act.

asr-000161
01:00:20.600 --> 01:00:36.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As we go through the budget, we want to know whether the resources being proposed for 2027 will allow DepDEP to fully perform its role in shaping our country's development, guiding government priorities, and helping improve the lives of our people.

asr-000162
01:00:37.040 --> 01:00:50.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: At the end of the day, the question is simple. Will this budget help DepDEP do its part in creating more jobs, reducing poverty, raising incomes, strengthening our economy, and giving Filipino families a better quality of life?

asr-000163
01:00:50.600 --> 01:01:00.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We hope that by the end of today's presentation and deliberations, the answer to that question will be a clear yes. Thank you very much.

