Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I mean, parang counterintuitive.

asr-001645
02:04:45.200 --> 02:04:46.720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Nag-Iran war.

asr-001646
02:04:46.980 --> 02:04:47.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Tumaas ang presyo.

asr-001647
02:04:47.920 --> 02:04:49.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Tumaas ng gasolina.

asr-001648
02:04:50.500 --> 02:04:52.500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Mataas ang inflation ng food.

asr-001649
02:04:54.500 --> 02:04:58.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Bumagsak ang poverty levels from last year.

asr-001650
02:04:58.640 --> 02:04:59.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Was it 16?

asr-001651
02:05:01.000 --> 02:05:01.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 15?

asr-001652
02:05:02.940 --> 02:05:03.940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Let me explain.

asr-001653
02:05:03.940 --> 02:05:04.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, go ahead.

asr-001654
02:05:04.760 --> 02:05:05.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, yes.

asr-001655
02:05:05.160 --> 02:05:06.460
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think that, yeah.

asr-001656
02:05:07.200 --> 02:05:15.360
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The data that we are capturing is 2023 versus 2025.

asr-001657
02:05:15.360 --> 02:05:17.680
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The data was 2025.

asr-001658
02:05:17.920 --> 02:05:18.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Not 2026.

asr-001659
02:05:18.920 --> 02:05:22.960
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The inflation in 2025 was very low.

asr-001660
02:05:23.140 --> 02:05:26.800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: 1.6%, something like that.

asr-001661
02:05:27.940 --> 02:05:31.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The 9.7% inflation is 2025.

asr-001662
02:05:32.200 --> 02:05:32.600
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: 2025.

asr-001663
02:05:32.900 --> 02:05:33.300
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Okay.

asr-001664
02:05:33.700 --> 02:05:35.300
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: That was the 9.7%.

asr-001665
02:05:35.300 --> 02:05:44.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And the decrease, comparing that with the conditions, economic conditions during that period, 2023 to 2025,

asr-001666
02:05:44.900 --> 02:06:02.620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: across income growths, or what's called income deciles, you see that households' incomes increased by almost, in nominal terms, over 20% in those periods.

asr-001667
02:06:02.620 --> 02:06:09.800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It was a period, quite unusual, I would say, because it was a period of low inflation.

asr-001668
02:06:10.840 --> 02:06:14.600
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Income growth was quite widespread across.

asr-001669
02:06:14.900 --> 02:06:16.520
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Households.

asr-001670
02:06:17.420 --> 02:06:20.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So it was not an inequitable growth.

asr-001671
02:06:22.220 --> 02:06:29.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: You can see the same percentage growth across the households' income classes.

asr-001672
02:06:31.420 --> 02:06:37.940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And yes, and the labor market was also at its best.

asr-001673
02:06:38.820 --> 02:06:43.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It was a period when unemployment was declining, underemployment was declining.

asr-001674
02:06:43.920 --> 02:07:05.020
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The 2026 is a different story because the Middle East conflict, the oil price, sharp price, oil price increases, the deceleration of growth because of the scandal, partly because of scandal and the high inflation.

asr-001675
02:07:05.420 --> 02:07:09.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So some of those gains could have been eroded.

asr-001676
02:07:10.160 --> 02:07:10.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Wipe out.

asr-001677
02:07:10.600 --> 02:07:13.020
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I don't think it is wipe out.

asr-001678
02:07:13.020 --> 02:07:15.060
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But I don't think, I really don't think that's wipe out.

asr-001679
02:07:15.400 --> 02:07:20.680
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But could have been eroded by those high inflation.

asr-001680
02:07:21.140 --> 02:07:28.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And now, unemployment is also beginning to, beginning, has also increased in recent quarters.

asr-001681
02:07:30.100 --> 02:07:32.940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Just one more question on the...

asr-001682
02:07:32.940 --> 02:07:35.920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, before it skips my mind, I follow up.

asr-001683
02:07:36.860 --> 02:07:42.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Where is the country headed in the next two years in terms of the, or using the following indicators?

asr-001684
02:07:43.020 --> 02:07:51.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Inflation, national debt, atsaka yung peso versus the U.S. dollar and other currencies?

asr-001685
02:07:53.820 --> 02:08:10.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The last one is quite difficult to know, Your Honor, because the value of the peso does not depend just on our actions, but also actions of other countries.

asr-001686
02:08:10.860 --> 02:08:12.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Now that the Fed is strengthening.

asr-001687
02:08:13.020 --> 02:08:26.280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It's raising its policy rates, you would expect a lot of pressure on the peso because dollar-denominated assets will become now much more attractive.

asr-001688
02:08:26.280 --> 02:08:42.540
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, but there are other, of course, factors that how investors and our local population, both consumers and producers, see the future.

asr-001689
02:08:43.020 --> 02:09:04.580
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And I think that if we can, as I keep saying, that if we can address the common variables that have led to this pessimism, to this negative sentiments that happened in the last quarters, three quarters, we could be on a recovery.

asr-001690
02:09:06.580 --> 02:09:12.580
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, I think that there are some good news.

asr-001691
02:09:13.020 --> 02:09:30.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: That happened lately, and I hope that that will temper now the sentiments, and I hope that there will are emerging solutions to the Middle East conflict, because that's the big uncertainty in the world economy right now.

asr-001692
02:09:31.540 --> 02:09:41.700
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We were expecting just a few months ago or a few weeks ago that oil prices would finally be at $80 per barrel.

asr-001693
02:09:41.700 --> 02:09:42.700
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But now it's back to...

asr-001694
02:09:43.020 --> 02:09:48.620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: To 100% because of, you know, certain actions that outside of our control.

asr-001695
02:09:48.800 --> 02:09:51.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, it's really a very uncertain world.

asr-001696
02:09:53.040 --> 02:09:55.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: You know, that's the least that I could say.

asr-001697
02:09:57.020 --> 02:10:02.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What's our projected national debt in June of 2028?

asr-001698
02:10:02.460 --> 02:10:07.120
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We are still working on a fiscal consolidation.

asr-001699
02:10:07.120 --> 02:10:12.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: As you can see in the budget, the budget, the increase in the budget was very...

asr-001700
02:10:13.020 --> 02:10:15.160
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Small.

asr-001701
02:10:15.340 --> 02:10:18.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: In fact, in real terms, it's likely flat.

asr-001702
02:10:18.780 --> 02:10:20.060
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It's more like a flat, no?

asr-001703
02:10:21.640 --> 02:10:30.820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Just to make sure that we are managing our fiscal issues, the fiscal space.

asr-001704
02:10:30.820 --> 02:10:41.820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And I think that we have agreed among the economic managers and discussed with the president that we need to...

asr-001705
02:10:43.020 --> 02:10:45.400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: To strong...

asr-001706
02:10:45.400 --> 02:10:52.660
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: To reorient our borrowing, to focus only on capital outlay and infrastructure, for example.

asr-001707
02:10:54.660 --> 02:10:55.260
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yeah.

asr-001708
02:10:56.060 --> 02:11:04.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Kasi parang [unclear] na tayo ng borrowing even for MOOE, ano?

asr-001709
02:11:04.840 --> 02:11:07.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I mean, some countries don't do that.

asr-001710
02:11:07.420 --> 02:11:09.260
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: They only borrow for capital outlay.

asr-001711
02:11:09.260 --> 02:11:12.260
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And I think that that's a direction that we should take.

asr-001712
02:11:12.520 --> 02:11:12.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And...

asr-001713
02:11:12.860 --> 02:11:13.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And...

asr-001715
02:11:13.020 --> 02:11:18.740
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: we are taking. And our fiscal consolidation program is geared for that.

asr-001716
02:11:19.340 --> 02:11:23.020
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Hopefully, there will be no extra pressure for us.

asr-001717
02:11:23.360 --> 02:11:27.240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The problem is really our vulnerability energy.

asr-001718
02:11:28.160 --> 02:11:37.620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Because we have little space that whenever, you know, world prices rise, we are hit quickly.

asr-001719
02:11:37.620 --> 02:11:42.620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Because we don't have the kind of energy situation that our neighbors...

asr-001720
02:11:43.020 --> 02:11:43.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: have.

asr-001721
02:11:44.760 --> 02:11:45.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Sir [unclear].

asr-001722
02:11:45.720 --> 02:11:46.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Thank you, Senator Kiko.

asr-001723
02:11:46.420 --> 02:11:46.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you.

asr-001724
02:11:46.800 --> 02:11:47.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, sir, Senator Pangilinan

asr-001725
02:11:47.200 --> 02:11:50.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Just a few more questions.

asr-001726
02:11:51.160 --> 02:11:52.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You know, we...

asr-001727
02:11:52.220 --> 02:11:53.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The anti-agric...

asr-001728
02:11:53.440 --> 02:11:54.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I just want to go back to that, no?

asr-001729
02:11:55.120 --> 02:11:56.080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Economic sabotage.

asr-001730
02:11:56.080 --> 02:12:01.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: May we request the DepDev to give us your position paper after two years.

asr-001731
02:12:02.880 --> 02:12:07.080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Unfortunately, you still don't have big-time smugglers being jailed.

asr-001732
02:12:11.320 --> 02:12:13.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And then, of course, the PCC.

asr-001733
02:12:13.020 --> 02:12:18.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The PCC Commission has yet to finalize its penalties on the Onion Cartel.

asr-001734
02:12:20.180 --> 02:12:31.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: There is a disconnect in the Council because it seems like the enforcement arm of the Council does not include the BOC and the DA.

asr-001735
02:12:33.060 --> 02:12:37.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And what I'm told is that kasi hindi mapagkatiwalaan yung dalawa.

asr-001736
02:12:37.960 --> 02:12:42.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They are in the Council, but they're not in the enforcement.

asr-001737
02:12:43.020 --> 02:12:46.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They're not in the enforcement entity.

asr-001738
02:12:47.100 --> 02:12:49.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I think that, you know...

asr-001739
02:12:51.700 --> 02:12:54.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They're the ones who know.

asr-001740
02:12:54.780 --> 02:12:56.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They're the ones who are guarding.

asr-001741
02:12:56.340 --> 02:12:57.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They're the ones mandated.

asr-001742
02:12:57.660 --> 02:13:08.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But when it comes to the enforcement for agri-smuggling, both the BOC and the DA are not in the enforcement bureau.

asr-001743
02:13:08.300 --> 02:13:12.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, can you give us a position?

asr-001744
02:13:13.020 --> 02:13:15.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I think it was an overreaction.

asr-001745
02:13:15.500 --> 02:13:17.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It was like a pendulum swing to the extreme.

asr-001746
02:13:18.460 --> 02:13:23.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dahil maraming smuggling, hindi nagagawa yung trabaho, et cetera.

asr-001747
02:13:23.280 --> 02:13:23.840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Huwag niyo isama.

asr-001748
02:13:25.020 --> 02:13:30.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Lalo gumulo yung sharing of information, et cetera.

asr-001749
02:13:31.680 --> 02:13:33.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi angkop.

asr-001750
02:13:34.880 --> 02:13:35.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Nagtuturoan pati.

asr-001751
02:13:36.540 --> 02:13:40.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, maybe the DepDev can give us your position paper.

asr-001752
02:13:41.140 --> 02:13:41.540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Let's...

asr-001753
02:13:41.540 --> 02:13:42.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Maybe you need to revisit that.

asr-001754
02:13:43.020 --> 02:13:46.380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That portion or provisions of the law.

asr-001755
02:13:46.460 --> 02:13:52.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kasi 10 milyon pesos lang ang kailangan para makakulong ng non-bailable offense.

asr-001756
02:13:53.200 --> 02:13:54.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 10 milyon pesos lang.

asr-001757
02:13:55.020 --> 02:13:58.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Panay ang announce ng gobyerno na billion ang nakukumpis ka.

asr-001758
02:13:59.000 --> 02:14:01.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 500 milyon dito ng sigarilyo.

asr-001759
02:14:03.700 --> 02:14:05.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 100 milyon ng karne.

asr-001760
02:14:07.900 --> 02:14:12.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pero, yung nakakulong, bodegero.

asr-001761
02:14:13.020 --> 02:14:17.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, ano nangyari ron?

asr-001762
02:14:18.400 --> 02:14:20.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sa halagang 10 milyon lang.

asr-001763
02:14:20.800 --> 02:14:21.720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Meron daw ilan.

asr-001764
02:14:23.140 --> 02:14:24.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But, that's not enough.

asr-001765
02:14:24.780 --> 02:14:32.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: If you're confiscating billions, then you should be jailing big-time smugglers.

asr-001766
02:14:32.940 --> 02:14:34.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: To the tune of billions.

asr-001767
02:14:34.600 --> 02:14:35.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, anyway, that one.

asr-001768
02:14:36.160 --> 02:14:38.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I'm sorry, I'm particular about that.

asr-001769
02:14:38.340 --> 02:14:42.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Because it's really killing our local agri

asr-001770
02:14:43.020 --> 02:14:45.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and fishery sector, when all these...

asr-001771
02:14:45.020 --> 02:14:48.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang malungkot pa doon, yung pinapasok na mga produkto,

asr-001772
02:14:49.020 --> 02:14:52.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: eh baka ano pa, siya salvage value.

asr-001773
02:14:52.220 --> 02:14:56.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kasi unfit na for human consumption doon sa China.

asr-001774
02:14:57.320 --> 02:14:58.920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dadalin dito, smuggled.

asr-001775
02:15:00.000 --> 02:15:03.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Tapos, sasabunin ng formalin,

asr-001776
02:15:03.940 --> 02:15:05.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: tapos ibebenta sa merkado.

asr-001777
02:15:06.320 --> 02:15:09.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, and then, when you look at all the,

asr-001778
02:15:09.620 --> 02:15:12.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: not all, but the items that are seized,

asr-001779
02:15:13.000 --> 02:15:14.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: unfit for human consumption,

asr-001780
02:15:14.560 --> 02:15:16.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: may E. coli, salmonella, etc.

asr-001781
02:15:17.700 --> 02:15:19.080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, well, anyway,

asr-001782
02:15:19.920 --> 02:15:21.840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: so maybe you can give us your position

asr-001783
02:15:21.840 --> 02:15:23.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: because we'd like to revisit the law

asr-001784
02:15:23.480 --> 02:15:27.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and provide the council with more teeth.

asr-001785
02:15:27.960 --> 02:15:30.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: My last question,

asr-001786
02:15:31.300 --> 02:15:32.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: or last two questions,

asr-001787
02:15:33.620 --> 02:15:36.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: the issue of, again, I go back to smuggling.

asr-001788
02:15:37.160 --> 02:15:38.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We had a hearing in March

asr-001789
02:15:38.800 --> 02:15:41.500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: regarding onion importation.

asr-001790
02:15:42.120 --> 02:15:47.880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The PSA had their projected harvest.

asr-001791
02:15:48.980 --> 02:15:50.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Senator Ping was there.

asr-001792
02:15:51.140 --> 02:15:53.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And then the BPI, DA,

asr-001793
02:15:53.500 --> 02:15:55.840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: had a different set of data.

asr-001794
02:15:57.960 --> 02:16:02.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The PSA had a lower requirement

asr-001795
02:16:02.700 --> 02:16:05.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: for the gap in terms of the supply deficit.

asr-001796
02:16:06.820 --> 02:16:08.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But the DA had a larger.

asr-001797
02:16:09.140 --> 02:16:09.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And therefore,

asr-001798
02:16:10.300 --> 02:16:12.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: nasunod yung DA,

asr-001799
02:16:13.900 --> 02:16:16.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: nag-import ng in excess,

asr-001800
02:16:16.800 --> 02:16:19.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: at least more than what PSA said.

asr-001801
02:16:20.380 --> 02:16:20.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So I said,

asr-001802
02:16:22.340 --> 02:16:23.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: we identified,

asr-001803
02:16:23.940 --> 02:16:27.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: we allocated 100 million for the PSA last year,

asr-001804
02:16:27.200 --> 02:16:27.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: for the PSA.

asr-001805
02:16:27.960 --> 02:16:30.060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The surveying and the research.

asr-001806
02:16:30.580 --> 02:16:31.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So I said,

asr-001807
02:16:31.380 --> 02:16:33.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: why don't you come up with a memorandum of agreement

asr-001808
02:16:33.480 --> 02:16:36.500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: between the DA and the PSA and the DepDev

asr-001809
02:16:36.500 --> 02:16:42.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: so that we have one set of data?

asr-001810
02:16:43.700 --> 02:16:44.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I'd like to think,

asr-001811
02:16:45.060 --> 02:16:45.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: DepDev,

asr-001812
02:16:46.320 --> 02:16:48.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I don't know.

asr-001813
02:16:48.860 --> 02:16:51.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But you're the researchers.

asr-001814
02:16:52.800 --> 02:16:54.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You're the statisticians.

asr-001815
02:16:54.780 --> 02:16:55.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That's not DA.

asr-001816
02:16:56.580 --> 02:16:57.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: DA should be the employer.

asr-001817
02:16:57.960 --> 02:16:58.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Implementor, et cetera.

asr-001818
02:17:00.200 --> 02:17:01.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So nagka-conflict sa datos,

asr-001819
02:17:02.940 --> 02:17:04.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: mas malaki yung data ng DA

asr-001820
02:17:04.480 --> 02:17:05.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: for some reason.

asr-001821
02:17:07.060 --> 02:17:08.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So nag-import ng mas malaki.

asr-001822
02:17:11.220 --> 02:17:11.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

asr-001823
02:17:12.580 --> 02:17:13.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Tapos sa panahon.

asr-001824
02:17:15.140 --> 02:17:18.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So can you clarify that?

asr-001825
02:17:18.460 --> 02:17:18.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, sir.

asr-001826
02:17:19.440 --> 02:17:20.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi I also,

asr-001827
02:17:20.600 --> 02:17:23.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I share the sentiment of Senator Pangilinan.

asr-001828
02:17:24.080 --> 02:17:26.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I authored the anti-agriculture smuglilo in 2016.

asr-001829
02:17:26.840 --> 02:17:28.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tapos nag-evolve,

asr-001830
02:17:28.680 --> 02:17:30.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: dati kasi smugling lang.

asr-001831
02:17:30.220 --> 02:17:31.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Nag-evolve naman.

asr-001832
02:17:32.080 --> 02:17:34.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Dahil nagkaroon ng gantong batas,

asr-001833
02:17:35.460 --> 02:17:38.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: left and right naman ang issuance ng importation permit.

asr-001834
02:17:38.440 --> 02:17:41.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya nga nag-agadag ng anti-agriculture economic sabotage ngayon.

asr-001835
02:17:41.780 --> 02:17:44.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That's the Conserve Center Pangilinan.

asr-001836
02:17:44.220 --> 02:17:49.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How can we do to improve better this one,

asr-001837
02:17:49.960 --> 02:17:53.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the reinforcement para magkaroon ng direksyon tungkol na natin?

asr-001838
02:17:53.400 --> 02:17:55.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sometimes it's frustrating to hear

asr-001839
02:17:55.540 --> 02:17:56.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the statement.

asr-001840
02:17:56.840 --> 02:17:57.760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The state of our agriculture,

asr-001841
02:17:58.000 --> 02:18:00.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: na talagang they import at the wrong time.

asr-001842
02:18:00.900 --> 02:18:01.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Di ba?

asr-001843
02:18:01.400 --> 02:18:02.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung patay,

asr-001844
02:18:02.700 --> 02:18:03.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: yung local industry natin,

asr-001845
02:18:03.840 --> 02:18:05.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: pinababayaan na ano na.

asr-001846
02:18:06.180 --> 02:18:08.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Parang napabayaan na import na na import.

asr-001847
02:18:08.400 --> 02:18:08.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So sige,

asr-001848
02:18:09.020 --> 02:18:10.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: we would like to hear from you.

asr-001849
02:18:11.420 --> 02:18:12.320
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Thank you,

asr-001850
02:18:12.580 --> 02:18:14.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Mr. Chair and Your Honor.

asr-001851
02:18:15.520 --> 02:18:17.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This is a long-standing issue.

asr-001852
02:18:18.440 --> 02:18:21.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Recall that before PSA was reorganized,

asr-001853
02:18:23.120 --> 02:18:25.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: there was a Bureau of Agricultural Statistics

asr-001854
02:18:25.340 --> 02:18:26.820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that collects data.

asr-001855
02:18:26.840 --> 02:18:28.560
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I would collect data.

asr-001856
02:18:29.620 --> 02:18:31.960
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But what,

asr-001857
02:18:32.200 --> 02:18:32.780
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and then PS,

asr-001858
02:18:33.040 --> 02:18:36.260
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the National Statistics Office

asr-001859
02:18:36.260 --> 02:18:38.240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: was also collecting data.

asr-001860
02:18:38.840 --> 02:18:42.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And those two data do not match,

asr-001861
02:18:42.160 --> 02:18:43.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: do not agree by a wide margin.

asr-001862
02:18:44.820 --> 02:18:48.480
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And there were many studies pointing to

asr-001863
02:18:48.480 --> 02:18:51.820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the need to integrate the two

asr-001864
02:18:51.820 --> 02:18:54.720
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: by removing the data collection

asr-001865
02:18:54.720 --> 02:18:56.720
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: for purposes of statistics.

asr-001866
02:18:56.840 --> 02:18:58.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Statistical compilation,

asr-001867
02:18:59.560 --> 02:19:01.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: especially compilation in support of

asr-001868
02:19:01.840 --> 02:19:03.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the national income accounts

asr-001869
02:19:03.760 --> 02:19:07.060
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: away from implementing agencies

asr-001870
02:19:07.060 --> 02:19:09.800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: so that there is a more credible

asr-001871
02:19:09.800 --> 02:19:16.260
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: sample-based statistically valid sampling methods

asr-001872
02:19:16.260 --> 02:19:18.320
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: applied so that the data

asr-001873
02:19:18.320 --> 02:19:20.320
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: are nationally representative.

asr-001874
02:19:21.000 --> 02:19:22.460
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So that was the decision.

asr-001875
02:19:23.240 --> 02:19:24.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But of course,

asr-001876
02:19:24.760 --> 02:19:25.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: over time,

asr-001877
02:19:26.840 --> 02:19:29.560
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the Department of Agriculture

asr-001878
02:19:29.560 --> 02:19:33.940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: realized that they still would have to collect

asr-001879
02:19:33.940 --> 02:19:37.560
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: their own data for administrative purposes.

asr-001880
02:19:38.380 --> 02:19:43.200
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And so that's where we are still at now.

asr-001881
02:19:43.300 --> 02:19:44.460
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But on the other hand,

asr-001882
02:19:44.800 --> 02:19:46.180
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: we have been,

asr-001883
02:19:47.480 --> 02:19:50.680
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think PSA and DA have been coordinating

asr-001884
02:19:50.680 --> 02:19:52.660
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: toward unifying their processes.

asr-001885
02:19:52.660 --> 02:19:53.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, because I asked them to.

asr-001886
02:19:53.860 --> 02:19:54.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And I told them,

asr-001887
02:19:55.660 --> 02:19:56.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: maybe,

asr-001888
02:19:56.840 --> 02:19:58.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and they acceded.

asr-001889
02:19:59.060 --> 02:19:59.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I said,

