Senator Erwin Tulfo: more investments

asr-002312
02:29:59.760 --> 02:30:00.680
Senator Erwin Tulfo: for this country.

asr-002313
02:30:00.680 --> 02:30:05.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: And I believe may mga naging, ah, uh,

asr-002314
02:30:05.000 --> 02:30:13.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Most of them were fruitful and it did happen, Mr. Secretary. So hindi naman nasayang yung pagbisita ng ating Pangulo.

asr-002315
02:30:13.180 --> 02:30:37.900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: My next question, sir, is would you happen to know na number, I don't know, I want to ask you this. I'm kind of surprised kasi there was a survey, sir, it says ito pong World Happiness Report 2026. Believe it or not, the Philippines ranks as the fourth happiest in Southeast Asia.

asr-002316
02:30:37.900 --> 02:30:43.060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I don't know for what reason bakit tayo happy and dami naman yung problema natin dito.

asr-002317
02:30:43.400 --> 02:31:00.740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Would you happen to know, ito ba yung nakarating na sa inyo, pinag-aaralan na ba ninyo bakit tayo rank fourth? Well, sa Southeast Asia. Pero overall po, sir, sa worldwide, pang 56 po tayo. Why is that?

asr-002318
02:31:01.740 --> 02:31:12.980
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: That's one metric that some people conceived to supplement or even.

asr-002319
02:31:13.180 --> 02:31:41.960
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Some to replace the traditional indicators like GDP, Mr. Chair. But usually the indicators are based on perceptions. So they're not quite strictly comparable to the traditional metrics that we have.

asr-002320
02:31:43.180 --> 02:32:03.980
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Like employment or inflation or GDP. It's more akin to, I believe, how social weather station surveys people's perception and the state of the economy or well-being, Mr. Chair.

asr-002321
02:32:03.980 --> 02:32:12.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, yeah, Butan is the one that has been the advocate of this.

asr-002322
02:32:13.180 --> 02:32:42.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Gross domestic happiness as a measure of well-being for countries. And there are some countries that actually want that idea, but still not part of the global mainstream for compilation of statistics.

asr-002323
02:32:43.180 --> 02:32:45.100
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Especially involving welfare.

asr-002324
02:32:45.940 --> 02:32:59.820
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kasi kung titignan mo, Mr. Secretary, sa social media, kung ano-ano sinasabi, parang wala ng pag-asa itong ating bayan. Kung anong-anong paninira na politika, et cetera, mahal na kuryente, mahal na bilihin.

asr-002325
02:32:59.820 --> 02:33:12.940
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Dapat it will, ika nga, yung ating minimum wage, et cetera. So, not that far with other countries. Pero, I don't know. I would appreciate it, sir.

asr-002326
02:33:13.180 --> 02:33:26.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: If you would look into this, I just want to find out why. Why are we ranked fourth happiest in Southeast Asia? We're the fourth, our people are the fourth happiest people in ASEAN, sir.

asr-002327
02:33:26.400 --> 02:33:37.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I will look into that and what data factors that they consider in compiling the data, Mr. Chair.

asr-002328
02:33:37.420 --> 02:33:40.060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: All right. I have another question, sir.

asr-002329
02:33:41.260 --> 02:33:43.140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I find the bill.

asr-002330
02:33:43.180 --> 02:34:07.920
Senator Erwin Tulfo: When I came here in the Senate last year, on the lifetime validity of PWD IDs, inincorporate na po ba ang PWID sa national ID? Kasi ito pong reklamo ng PWDs. Every year or two years or three years, they have to go to the city hall, to the munisipyo. They have to travel, lalo na po yung may problema sa mobility.

asr-002331
02:34:09.100 --> 02:34:13.040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Inconvenient nga naman. So, I filed a bill na maging gawin na po.

asr-002332
02:34:13.180 --> 02:34:23.780
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Itong lifetime. Habang nabubuhay yung PWD, tawag na siya mag-renew na mag-renew. Dahil kita naman, may kapansanang, putol ang paa, etc. na makalakad.

asr-002333
02:34:26.020 --> 02:34:30.740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Na-incorporate ba ito sa national ID or wala pa po? Wala pang plano dito?

asr-002334
02:34:43.180 --> 02:34:55.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Mr. Chair, it's now under discussion with the National Council of Disability Affairs. I think it's with the board.

asr-002335
02:34:56.040 --> 02:35:01.960
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And once we have that recommendation, we'll pass it on to PSA for action.

asr-002336
02:35:01.960 --> 02:35:13.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: All right. Thank you, Mr. Secretary. Another point I want to raise with you, your office. I also filed a bill on Philippine Oil Reserve.

asr-002337
02:35:14.000 --> 02:35:22.540
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Maaaring po bang malaman ang posisyon po ng DepDev? How will this strongly help our country's economy in terms of oil shortage?

asr-002338
02:35:23.140 --> 02:35:30.840
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Actually, I've been speaking to some of the representatives of ADNOC in Abu Dhabi.

asr-002339
02:35:31.480 --> 02:35:41.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: They're very willing, Mr. Secretary, to put up storage facilities. Matter of fact, they want to put up storage facilities in Luzon, Visayas, and Mindanao.

asr-002340
02:35:41.000 --> 02:35:57.960
Senator Erwin Tulfo: All we have to do is we have to come up or we have to identify an area where they can put the storage facilities. Depende daw po sa ating kung gano'ng kalaki. And they're looking at around 50 million barrels they want to store.

asr-002341
02:35:57.960 --> 02:36:14.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So kung malalagyan. Pero when we were computing, it's a Department of Energy, it will take like about 500 hectares for that 50 million barrels. Because we consume like around 450,000 barrels per day.

asr-002342
02:36:15.060 --> 02:36:26.600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Saudi Arabia is also, Aramco is also interested, Mr. Secretary, in the same deal. Bahala po tayo sa lupa, sila po ang magkukonstruct.

asr-002343
02:36:26.600 --> 02:36:44.960
Senator Erwin Tulfo: No money out po sa atin. Pati yung reserve po, yung fuel, ilalagay po nila. Well, double purpose din po sa kanila yun para kung magkakaroon na naman ng gera or something to that effect like closing Strait of Hormuz, Arabian Sea, etc.

asr-002344
02:36:45.240 --> 02:36:55.860
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Meron na po silang pagkukunan na labas sa country nila. That's what their plans are. And then, what do we get out of it will be the first priority.

asr-002345
02:36:55.860 --> 02:37:21.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, number two, hindi naman totally bawaba na malaki yung price. Pero may konting effect because hindi na po itatransport kung meron na po mga storage facilities. I believe DOE also is making or talking with Japan, Ministry of Energy, METI.

asr-002346
02:37:21.080 --> 02:37:24.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, yun po. Yung tatlong...

asr-002347
02:37:25.860 --> 02:37:32.320
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Aspect po na yun. Yun ang tanong ko sa inyo. Anong position nyo rito, Secretary?

asr-002348
02:37:32.320 --> 02:37:53.320
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think the cost of energy and security, Mr. Chair, Your Honor, is very, very high as we have experienced it. So, we should explore options like what you're...

asr-002349
02:37:55.860 --> 02:38:25.240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: proposing, Your Honor. And this one that's the most fiscally and economically viable. Of course, even for oil reserve storage, there are possibly other ways of achieving that. And we need to look at what is the most advantageous, especially from a fiscal point of view.

asr-002350
02:38:25.860 --> 02:38:39.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Space viewpoint because our fiscal space is so challenging. And we should undertake such measure.

asr-002351
02:38:39.860 --> 02:38:43.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Of course, there are other things that...

asr-002352
02:38:51.860 --> 02:38:55.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Other things that we need to do.

asr-002353
02:38:55.860 --> 02:39:21.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: To complement that measure, Mr. Chair, like increasing the mix of our energy. It should be seriously considered too because we are so vulnerable in having just a few sources. I'm talking about, for example, the need to perhaps even consider nuclear energy to the extent that these are

asr-002354
02:39:21.860 --> 02:39:47.960
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: technologically manageable. And we can assure of the safety of such technology because that's very cheap also from a source of energy. And so, yeah, I completely agree. We should move into diversifying our sources and making sure that we need the power when we need the most.

asr-002355
02:39:48.540 --> 02:39:51.840
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Mr. Secretary, I believe on your next cabinet meeting, you might want to...

asr-002356
02:39:51.880 --> 02:39:56.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I'm going to have to inform or remind the President because I believe on his visit in Dubai,

asr-002357
02:39:56.480 --> 02:40:08.820
Senator Erwin Tulfo: he was already informed of their interest in building storage facilities. I believe Secretary Garin was also informed about it.

asr-002358
02:40:09.140 --> 02:40:20.420
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, and just recently, Saudi Arabia also made a proposal wherein they want to build storage facilities. If we have all these countries' storage facilities,

asr-002359
02:40:20.420 --> 02:40:28.960
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I guess we won't have any problems. Hindi po tayo kakaba-kaba pag nagkaroon po ng mga gera in the very near future dahil nandito po yung kanilang facilities.

asr-002360
02:40:29.600 --> 02:40:38.440
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Another thing, Mr. Secretary, I want to bring to your attention. I don't know. Gusto ko sanang paimbestigahan because I'm the chairman of the Committee on Energy.

asr-002361
02:40:39.020 --> 02:40:49.220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Unfortunately, we're in the process of conducting impeachment trial and then meron po kami budget hearing. But I really would love to get my hands on this issue.

asr-002362
02:40:50.420 --> 02:41:05.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: About our electricity rate. I found out, Mr. Secretary, maybe your office, maybe you can help us out. You can help my committee look into this because we have a problem with our power.

asr-002363
02:41:05.500 --> 02:41:19.900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It's one of the most expensive or the most expensive in the sea. But Mr. Secretary, when I did my research a couple of days ago, about 60% of our power, electricity, the source is coal.

asr-002364
02:41:20.340 --> 02:41:20.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: 60%.

asr-002365
02:41:20.420 --> 02:41:34.140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: About 10% to 15% is a bunker fuel. Pero how come the rate is so high, Mr. Secretary? And so I looked into it and I saw the problem.

asr-002366
02:41:34.960 --> 02:41:47.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We get most of our coal from Jakarta. It's like 3 pesos per kilowatt hour. Bunker fuel per kilowatt hour is like about 25, 35 pesos. So there's a big difference.

asr-002367
02:41:47.300 --> 02:42:01.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: 3 pesos po itong isa. 35 po itong isa. Pero pag dumating na po sa WESEM, sa spot market, pumapantay na po yung coal.

asr-002368
02:42:02.380 --> 02:42:13.780
Senator Erwin Tulfo: At ang reason, kasi daw yung shipment. And I don't think, Mr. Secretary, na from 3 pesos, aabot sa 35 pesos ang coal dahil sa shipment.

asr-002369
02:42:15.240 --> 02:42:17.220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Pinapantay po. Nagkakaproblema po tayo sa WESEM.

asr-002370
02:42:17.220 --> 02:42:33.420
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Sa spot market. Pumapantay po yung 3 pesos na coal sa bunker fuel. I guess if we can address this issue, if we can call the attention of WESEM, and probably the ERC can help us out, control this.

asr-002371
02:42:33.940 --> 02:42:46.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I believe, Mr. Secretary, magiging affordable kahit papano yung electricity natin. Hindi po, sir. Ang ginagawa po sa spot market, dito po yung bunker fuel, dito po yung coal.

asr-002372
02:42:46.080 --> 02:42:53.720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Pinapantay po nila. You get what I mean? Wala na po yung difference eh.

asr-002373
02:42:54.280 --> 02:43:00.320
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Eh dapat po mas mura dahil coal po tayo. Hindi naman po bunker. Bunker is only 15%.

asr-002374
02:43:00.320 --> 02:43:12.160
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We use like about 60%. So maybe, Mr. Secretary, through your office, maybe you can call the attention of the WESEM para po ikang matignan po ito.

asr-002375
02:43:12.160 --> 02:43:14.640
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Because there's really a big disparity, Mr. Secretary.

asr-002376
02:43:16.080 --> 02:43:22.620
Senator Erwin Tulfo: And if we can do something about this, I guess we can bring the electricity rate down, Secretary Balisakan.

asr-002377
02:43:24.880 --> 02:43:26.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Look into it, sir.

asr-002378
02:43:27.100 --> 02:43:42.140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, sir. That's what we found out recently. And I was informed by my contacts in the Energy Department na yan nga daw po ang problema.

asr-002379
02:43:42.140 --> 02:43:43.360
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Alright, sir.

asr-002380
02:43:46.080 --> 02:44:12.920
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Under the 2025 COA report, Mr. Secretary, the NEDA Building Improvement Project, Phase 1, 2, and 3, with a combined contract cost of 641.556 million, remain not completed due to risk, contingencies, and other circumstances not adequately considered by both the agency and the contractor.

asr-002381
02:44:13.760 --> 02:44:16.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Resulting in project delays.

asr-002382
02:44:16.080 --> 02:44:40.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Resulting in project delays and multiple contract amendments, extensions, which affected the timely delivery of intended benefits to end-users. Moreover, payment for variation orders arising from the erroneous as found plans submitted by the contractor resulted in increased costs to the agency and further contributed to delays in project completion.

asr-002385
02:44:40.960 --> 02:44:49.100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: May project delays po ang NEDA building, improvement project with a combined contract cost worth 641 million.

asr-002386
02:44:49.900 --> 02:44:52.720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Madaming contract amendments and extensions.

asr-002387
02:44:53.640 --> 02:44:58.060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Naayos na po ba itong problema na ito, Mr. Secretary?

asr-002388
02:45:00.000 --> 02:45:18.400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yes, Mr. Chair, but I have my Undersecretary Monica Pagunsan here who is in charge of our building project to brief you on that.

asr-002389
02:45:18.400 --> 02:45:44.780
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But what you mentioned is correct. We only found later after digging the basement for the basement of the building that the structure of the building adjacent to what we are trying to build was not stable because I believe some defects in the earlier construction.

asr-002390
02:45:44.780 --> 02:45:48.380
Senator Erwin Tulfo: What is the problem initially on your investment?

asr-002391
02:45:48.400 --> 02:46:01.860
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Before we go to the Undersecretary, I don't have any problem as a design. Is it the contractor's fault trying to save money? What is it?

asr-002392
02:46:01.860 --> 02:46:17.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: No, I believe what happened, the design was correct, Your Honor. But when the contractor, after digging the grounds, where the building would be put up is just…

asr-002393
02:46:18.400 --> 02:46:48.180
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It was adjacent to an existing building and it turned out that the walls for that older building was quite weak and unstable so that the contractor was so concerned that that might collapse and so they had to do some remediation to prevent possible collapse of the walls.

asr-002394
02:46:48.400 --> 02:46:53.640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But Monica knows the details better than I do.

asr-002395
02:46:54.800 --> 02:46:57.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Go ahead, Undersecretary, ma'am. Go ahead.

asr-002396
02:46:57.920 --> 02:47:09.780
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: Mr. Chair and Senator Tulfo, first of all, we have two constructions. One is for the renovation of the old building.

asr-002397
02:47:11.620 --> 02:47:18.380
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: That was a renovation that does not really have… we don't really have visibility because we don't…

asr-002398
02:47:18.400 --> 02:47:35.420
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: We don't have the as-built plan. So that when you go into the renovation process, you eventually find some things that were not really visible during the inspection, which really have to do an investigation.

asr-002399
02:47:36.560 --> 02:47:42.980
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: But these are only minor, no? But we really have to correct them.

asr-002400
02:47:44.160 --> 02:47:47.980
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: Another one is there was a delay because at that time…

asr-002401
02:47:48.400 --> 02:47:56.020
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: We have asked for help from DPWH to retrofit that old building.

asr-002402
02:47:57.140 --> 02:48:02.420
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: There was a… and that was a contract entered into by DPWH.

asr-002403
02:48:02.420 --> 02:48:16.560
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: That is why when DPWH was doing the retrofitting, we did not accept the result, no?

asr-002404
02:48:16.560 --> 02:48:17.560
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: Of the first…

asr-002405
02:48:18.400 --> 02:48:30.440
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: The completion. In other words, we did not accept the project. That was why there was also a delay in the execution of the renovation.

asr-002406
02:48:31.680 --> 02:48:37.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya nga, ma'am, saan ho naging problema? Lack of foresight? Kanino pong kasalanan? Is it the contractor?

asr-002407
02:48:37.080 --> 02:48:47.840
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Of course, when you do renovation, Undersecretary, there will be plans. Good thing po, nakita ho ninyo bago may madisgrasya, di po ba may mamatay.

asr-002408
02:48:48.400 --> 02:49:03.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kunting lindo lang ho yan. Tama si Secretary. Baka may mga masaktan. So, it was good. Pero my question is, lack of foresight? Yung planning? O yung ikang drawing ng architect?

asr-002409
02:49:03.080 --> 02:49:09.900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I mean, they should have submitted plans for the repair, Undersecretary.

asr-002410
02:49:10.480 --> 02:49:17.800
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: There are really cases, Senator, that we really have to rely on as-built plans.

asr-002411
02:49:18.400 --> 02:49:28.460
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: Unfortunately, there was none. We can no longer find the as-built plan which was done in 19… I mean, the building was built in 1972.

asr-002412
02:49:28.740 --> 02:49:43.740
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: We cannot find that. So that, when we came up with a plan, we were not able to see certain issues that still needs to be addressed.

asr-002413
02:49:44.480 --> 02:49:47.460
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: But really, the main delay there was that the implementation…

asr-002414
02:49:48.400 --> 02:49:59.240
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: The implementation of the retrofitting, which we cannot also go ahead. We had to complete the retrofitting first before we can continue with the execution of the plan.

asr-002415
02:49:59.240 --> 02:50:18.240
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: Which we consider na there was really no… The plan was alright. It's in order. However, the delay really was on.

asr-002416
02:50:18.240 --> 02:50:36.700
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: On the retrofitting, and as well as certain areas that we need to correct in the design of the building based on the as-found when we did a deeper investigation of the project.

asr-002417
02:50:37.340 --> 02:50:47.680
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: So, we did our best. I think there was… Our designers did… They may not have anticipated this.

asr-002418
02:50:47.680 --> 02:51:05.000
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: However, dahil as-found… We did not find it during the design stage. Dahil it's… You really have to open up the certain areas before you do remediation.

asr-002419
02:51:05.560 --> 02:51:17.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kasi ma'am, kung may mga… Kung ang problem po ninyo, yung pagiging stable ng building when you construct it, meron po dapat ikaw nga mga tinatawag tayo na soil.

asr-002420
02:51:17.680 --> 02:51:33.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ito ba yung malambot? Kasi may mga projects po tayo, take the case of that skyway they built in Iloilo, sagging po at sumasayaw-sayaw ngayon because hindi po sila nag-soil test.

asr-002421
02:51:33.480 --> 02:51:47.120
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya yung foundation ng tulay ko sa Iloilo, gumaganoon. Under investigation nga din po. Kasama po yun dyan sa flood control issue. Kasi nga po yung contractor iniimbestigahan na ngayon dahil hindi nga po stable.

asr-002422
02:51:47.680 --> 02:52:04.360
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Wala po bang ginawang soil test ang ika nga contractor o yung engineers na ika nga nagagawa po ng building na yan para ika nga masiguro na safe po na magtayo ng building dyan?

asr-002423
02:52:06.520 --> 02:52:16.720
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: We did have a soil testing, Mr. Chair, but really… And we did even go into the investigation of the entire building, of the old building.

asr-002424
02:52:17.680 --> 02:52:23.020
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: And that was also the basis for the design, for the structural design of the building.

asr-002425
02:52:23.740 --> 02:52:34.080
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: It's just that naabutan po kami. We had to retrofit and strengthen the foundation of the old building.

asr-002426
02:52:37.880 --> 02:52:47.020
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: Yung nare-refer po ng kuha namin, it's on the size of the particular…

asr-002427
02:52:47.680 --> 02:53:02.580
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: Building. I mean, the size of that particular area wherein we really do have to make some variation order because of as found nga na po na we need to address.

asr-002428
02:53:03.080 --> 02:53:06.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So ano hong status ngayon ng construction po na yan? Naka-hold po?

asr-002429
02:53:06.940 --> 02:53:15.700
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: No, sir. We are now at the… There are different phases kasi. For the first phase, we're already on 96%.

asr-002430
02:53:17.680 --> 02:53:37.680
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: For the second phase… No, sorry. For the first phase, it's 90.75%. For the second phase, it's at 96.67%.

asr-002431
02:53:37.680 --> 02:53:46.680
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: And the last phase, it's at 87.06%. That is as of August…

asr-002432
02:53:47.680 --> 02:53:59.240
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: Ah, September 30, 2026. And we are looking at… September 30 pala, sorry.

asr-002433
02:54:03.120 --> 02:54:15.220
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: August 31, 2026. And we are expecting to transfer by January, Mr. Senator Tulfo.

asr-002434
02:54:15.220 --> 02:54:17.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: All right, ma'am. I'm satisfied.

asr-002435
02:54:17.680 --> 02:54:19.780
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I'm satisfied with your answer. Parang kinakabahan ho kayo.

asr-002436
02:54:20.060 --> 02:54:25.060
DEPDev Undersecretary Ma. Monica P. Pagunsan: Kinakabahan ho talaga ako. Kaya I was not expecting that I'm going to answer this question.

asr-002437
02:54:25.220 --> 02:54:32.780
Senator Erwin Tulfo: You blame Secretary Balisakan. Anyway, going back to you, Secretary Balisakan, sir.

asr-002438
02:54:34.320 --> 02:54:45.840
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Last August 2026, I don't know if this was already asked kanina by my colleagues, the Senate created the Reinvigorate Investment and Sustainable Economic Growth or RISE.

asr-002439
02:54:47.680 --> 02:55:04.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ad-hoc committee to address the recent slowdown in the Philippine economy. I am the vice chair of this ad-hoc committee, Mr. Secretary. May mga nakikita ba kayong legislative reforms and long-term policy interventions aimed at sustainable economic growth?

asr-002440
02:55:08.400 --> 02:55:16.400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We have, Your Honor, the LEDAC, the Reform…

asr-002441
02:55:17.680 --> 02:55:34.800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Our legislative list of LEDAC reflect the priorities of the administration to speed up recovery and sustain economic development, Your Honor.

asr-002442
02:55:34.800 --> 02:55:46.800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It's a long list, but about 23 of those are committed by both houses of Congress, by the leaders of the both houses.

asr-002443
02:55:47.680 --> 02:55:56.060
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And the executive to pass by June of next year. Hopefully, we get…

asr-002444
02:55:56.060 --> 02:56:06.280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: One of those, for example, is on the energy, the amendment to the EPIRA, Your Honor, to address this high cost of power.

asr-002445
02:56:06.280 --> 02:56:16.280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The others have to do with improving accountability and transparency, access to…

asr-002446
02:56:17.680 --> 02:56:32.220
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Information that we believe will help improve the sentiment of our people, particularly the investing community and our economy.

asr-002447
02:56:32.960 --> 02:56:47.220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Mr. Chair, I mean, Mr. Secretary, is it true because of the economy slowed down last year because of our expenses, government spending, particularly in construction?

asr-002448
02:56:47.680 --> 02:56:54.160
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Dahil nga po, ang center of attention was the flood control by the public works and highways, so nag-slow down.

asr-002449
02:56:55.240 --> 02:57:07.720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Do you think we will do better this year? I mean, the Senate is funding now construction, I mean, funds for infrastructure by the public works and highways by next year, 2027.

asr-002450
02:57:08.080 --> 02:57:15.780
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Do you think it will greatly help? Because right now, sir, last year or this year, talaga nag-slow down po yung ating economy.

asr-002451
02:57:17.680 --> 02:57:43.640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Definitely, Your Honor, because the last two quarters, at least, saw a sharp contraction of public investments, particularly related to the infrastructure, and that easily cleaved off at least one percentage point growth of GDP.

asr-002452
02:57:43.640 --> 02:57:46.640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It's quite an enormous impact.

asr-002453
02:57:47.680 --> 02:58:09.320
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Then if you combine that with the effects of the Middle East conflict, which led to sharp increases in inflation, that substantially tempered down the sentiments of consumers,

asr-002454
02:58:09.320 --> 02:58:17.440
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: because those combinations of high prices and lower income growth…

asr-002455
02:58:17.680 --> 02:58:47.240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Both meant that their purchasing power was badly affected, and so that, if you look at the consumption side of the economy, also explained the slowdown, because the consumption is a big part of the economy, it's almost a two-third of the economy is just in the consumption, and that slowed down substantially as a result of this weak sentiments of the investment.

asr-002456
02:58:47.680 --> 02:59:09.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And because private sector infrastructure or private sector investment is also very much related with public sector investment, when the public sector investment collapsed, the private sector was also affected severely.

asr-002457
02:59:09.840 --> 02:59:16.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, all this put together led to the situation where we are…

asr-002458
02:59:17.680 --> 02:59:27.400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But I believe that we are starting to recover, Mr. Chair.

asr-002459
02:59:30.400 --> 02:59:46.400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Our colleagues in DBM assured us that the releases of budgets of all agencies and the current pace of disbursements…

asr-002460
02:59:47.680 --> 03:00:00.560
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Of contracts, or at least for those that have no, with clear records, could go, and that should…

asr-002461
03:00:00.560 --> 03:00:05.460
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: allow us to see recovery of construction.

asr-002462
03:00:06.220 --> 03:00:11.440
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And you can imagine the amount of construction that could happen

asr-002463
03:00:11.440 --> 03:00:14.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: because last two quarters, as I said,

asr-002464
03:00:14.540 --> 03:00:20.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: we had almost like 30% contraction per quarter.

asr-002465
03:00:21.160 --> 03:00:25.100
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And all those unspent money there would have to now be spent

asr-002466
03:00:25.100 --> 03:00:31.200
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: in the last quarter of, at least in the last quarter of this year,

asr-002467
03:00:31.460 --> 03:00:34.640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: plus their budget for this year, for this quarter.

asr-002468
03:00:34.820 --> 03:00:38.740
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So you have enormous resources that would have to be mobilized.

asr-002469
03:00:39.860 --> 03:00:45.540
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And so if our infrastructure agencies, particularly DPWH,

asr-002470
03:00:45.540 --> 03:00:50.740
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: but also the DepEd for their school classrooms,

asr-002471
03:00:51.820 --> 03:00:54.780
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: DA for their farm-to-market roads and irrigation,

asr-002472
03:00:55.100 --> 03:00:58.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and so on, there's a lot of that, Mr. Chair.

asr-002473
03:00:59.240 --> 03:01:00.380
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Secretary.

asr-002474
03:01:00.780 --> 03:01:04.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Mr. Chair, before I go back to the plenary,

asr-002475
03:01:04.780 --> 03:01:09.200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I would just like to tell this body that I support

asr-002476
03:01:09.200 --> 03:01:12.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: for the passage of the budget of the DEP-DEV.

asr-002477
03:01:15.060 --> 03:01:20.260
Senator Erwin Tulfo: And if there is any more or anything that they would like to add on,

asr-002478
03:01:20.360 --> 03:01:21.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: we will see at the plenary.

asr-002479
03:01:22.640 --> 03:01:24.660
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So I will be supporting, rest assured,

asr-002480
03:01:25.100 --> 03:01:27.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I support, Mr. Secretary,

asr-002481
03:01:27.340 --> 03:01:32.240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: for the passage of this budget for 2027 of the DEP-DEV.

asr-002482
03:01:32.360 --> 03:01:33.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Secretary.

asr-002483
03:01:34.220 --> 03:01:35.520
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-002484
03:01:35.660 --> 03:01:37.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Erwin Tulfo.

asr-002485
03:01:39.220 --> 03:01:42.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Anyway, going back to what we discussed,

asr-002486
03:01:42.180 --> 03:01:46.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I was interested in the query of Senator Tulfo.

asr-002487
03:01:48.360 --> 03:01:52.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That's why this budget season,

asr-002488
03:01:52.180 --> 03:01:55.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: we really have to accelerate spending and growth.

asr-002489
03:01:55.100 --> 03:01:57.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So that we will be able to play catch-up.

asr-002490
03:01:57.760 --> 03:02:00.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Talagang malaki-laki nga abuli natin.

asr-002491
03:02:01.820 --> 03:02:02.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Is ito, no?

asr-002492
03:02:02.740 --> 03:02:07.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tama, 2% lang tayong GDP this year compared to 4% last year, Secretary?

asr-002493
03:02:07.760 --> 03:02:12.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: 4.4 tayo for the full year next year.

asr-002494
03:02:12.520 --> 03:02:16.100
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We're still hoping to get at least the low end of our target,

asr-002495
03:02:16.960 --> 03:02:18.480
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: which is 3.5 to 4.5.

asr-002496
03:02:18.620 --> 03:02:19.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The low end is 3.5.

asr-002497
03:02:19.820 --> 03:02:23.960
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: If we can get as close as possible to the lower end,

asr-002498
03:02:23.960 --> 03:02:24.940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think that will be half.

asr-002499
03:02:25.100 --> 03:02:27.720
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Happy because the first two quarters

asr-002500
03:02:27.720 --> 03:02:31.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: are already, you know, continue to be...

asr-002501
03:02:31.340 --> 03:02:36.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Talagang grabe effect sa atin nung itong flood control.

asr-002502
03:02:36.860 --> 03:02:38.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: More than a year already.

asr-002503
03:02:39.120 --> 03:02:40.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And we're still reeling from it.

asr-002504
03:02:40.920 --> 03:02:44.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Hopefully, baka yung ating public spending

asr-002505
03:02:44.960 --> 03:02:47.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: will be able to catch up.

asr-002506
03:02:48.180 --> 03:02:49.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sana itong third quarter,

asr-002507
03:02:49.660 --> 03:02:51.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: pero maka-aabot pa ng third and fourth, no?

asr-002508
03:02:52.380 --> 03:02:53.520
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Third quarter siguro.

asr-002509
03:02:54.220 --> 03:02:54.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Maka-aabot.

asr-002510
03:02:55.100 --> 03:02:55.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Hopefully.

asr-002511
03:02:56.400 --> 03:02:56.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Hopefully.

asr-002512
03:02:57.040 --> 03:02:58.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That's why yung sabi ko nga dito, Sec,

asr-002513
03:02:59.300 --> 03:03:01.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: you have to strike a balance right now.

asr-002514
03:03:01.660 --> 03:03:03.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Although, of course, we are for accountability

asr-002515
03:03:03.740 --> 03:03:05.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: dun sa mga nagkasala,

asr-002516
03:03:06.040 --> 03:03:07.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the biggest scandal ever.

asr-002517
03:03:08.660 --> 03:03:12.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But we need to accelerate the growth also

asr-002518
03:03:12.180 --> 03:03:14.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: through increased public spending.

asr-002519
03:03:16.140 --> 03:03:17.780
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We agree, Mr. Chair.

asr-002520
03:03:18.960 --> 03:03:21.760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I'll just have a few questions, Secretary.

asr-002521
03:03:22.020 --> 03:03:23.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Just take note of the, ano na lang, no?

asr-002522
03:03:23.960 --> 03:03:24.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung mga...

asr-002523
03:03:25.100 --> 03:03:30.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung mga issues and concerns of the Senators

asr-002524
03:03:30.920 --> 03:03:35.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: so that we can prepare for the plenary debates.

asr-002525
03:03:35.900 --> 03:03:39.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Malamang baka matanong ulit or may follow-up.

asr-002526
03:03:39.620 --> 03:03:41.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, sa mga agencies concerned,

asr-002527
03:03:42.000 --> 03:03:43.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: sa mga USEC, ASSEC,

asr-002528
03:03:43.400 --> 03:03:45.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: please prepare for those.

asr-002529
03:03:47.040 --> 03:03:49.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Doon sa Regional Development Councils,

asr-002530
03:03:49.360 --> 03:03:52.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ito po, amount of 164 million is appropriated

asr-002531
03:03:52.580 --> 03:03:54.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to the Regional Development Councils

asr-002532
03:03:54.120 --> 03:03:54.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: for the provision of support.

asr-002533
03:03:55.100 --> 03:03:57.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Services to RDCs,

asr-002534
03:03:57.600 --> 03:03:59.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: as well as monitoring and evaluation

asr-002535
03:03:59.340 --> 03:04:03.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: of the implementation of plans, programs, policies, projects.

asr-002536
03:04:04.300 --> 03:04:07.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Given the recent issues involving flood control projects,

asr-002537
03:04:07.520 --> 03:04:11.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: how can DEP-DEV strengthen the role of Regional Development Councils

asr-002538
03:04:11.860 --> 03:04:12.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: in the planning process?

asr-002539
03:04:13.580 --> 03:04:17.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Not only in identifying and prioritizing infrastructure projects,

asr-002540
03:04:17.040 --> 03:04:21.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: but also in ensuring that projects are implementation-ready,

asr-002541
03:04:22.740 --> 03:04:24.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: monitoring of actual implementation,

asr-002542
03:04:24.040 --> 03:04:27.600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and what projects should continue to receive funding.

asr-002543
03:04:29.500 --> 03:04:31.800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-002544
03:04:31.800 --> 03:04:38.820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We appreciate the support given to the RDCs last year's budget.

asr-002545
03:04:40.120 --> 03:04:45.180
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And we hope that we can get additional resources for the RDCs

asr-002546
03:04:45.180 --> 03:04:52.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: because the RDCs are not DEP-DEV, Mr. Chair.

asr-002547
03:04:53.120 --> 03:04:53.800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We coordinate...

asr-002548
03:04:54.040 --> 03:04:56.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We are the services secretariat to the RDCs,

asr-002549
03:04:56.500 --> 03:05:03.480
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: but what constrain the RDCs are the resources available

asr-002550
03:05:03.480 --> 03:05:06.600
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: for coordination, mobilization,

asr-002551
03:05:07.740 --> 03:05:13.540
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and with more resources,

asr-002552
03:05:13.540 --> 03:05:21.960
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: we could improve the performance of our RDCs,

asr-002553
03:05:22.020 --> 03:05:23.540
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: particularly in ensuring that...

asr-002554
03:05:24.040 --> 03:05:31.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that there are enough implementation-ready projects

asr-002555
03:05:31.500 --> 03:05:34.240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: identified at the regional level,

asr-002556
03:05:34.360 --> 03:05:39.200
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and these are also consistent with the priorities at the national level.

asr-002557
03:05:40.260 --> 03:05:43.280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And as you must have seen,

asr-002558
03:05:43.520 --> 03:05:47.940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the table of Senator Gatchel Jan, Your Honor,

asr-002559
03:05:47.940 --> 03:05:53.700
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: where he showed that only about 40%, roughly,

asr-002560
03:05:54.040 --> 03:05:55.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: or even less,

asr-002561
03:05:56.100 --> 03:05:59.620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: of the high-priority projects of our RDCs

asr-002562
03:05:59.620 --> 03:06:05.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: are reflected in the NEP.

asr-002563
